meta {
  name: Create OTP (ResetPwd)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{ACCOUNTS_APIS_BASE_URL}}/auth/create-code
  body: none
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
      "email": "{{MY_EMAIL}}",
      "requestType": "ResetPwd"
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  req.setBody({
    email: bru.getGlobalEnvVar("MY_EMAIL"),
    requestType: "ResetPwd"
  })
}

script:post-response {
  if(res.getStatus() == 200){
      bru.setGlobalEnvVar(
        "VERIFICATION_CODE_ID", 
        res.getBody().data.verificationCodeId
      );
  }
}

docs {
  This endpoint is used to generate an OTP (One-Time Password) for the purpose of resetting a user's password. The OTP will be sent to the user's registered email address. Once the OTP is verified, a one-time use JWT will be generated, allowing the user to reset their password securely.
  
  #### **Steps to Reset Password**
  1. **Call the `Create OTP (ResetPwd)` Endpoint**: This sends an OTP to the user's registered email address for verification.
  
  2. **Call `Verify OTP (ResetPwd)` Endpoint**: Use the OTP received in the email with the `/auth/verify-code` endpoint. Set `requestType` to `"ResetPwd"` in the verification request. Upon successful verification, a one-time JWT is issued.
  
  4. **Call the `Reset Password` Endpoint**: Use the one-time JWT to reset the password securely.
  
  > Note: This endpoint always returns a success response regardless of the actual outcome. This is done for security reasons and the client will not be informed of the specific result.
}
